[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=UDP Census v1.0\\\\One 4-Series symbol that can answer a processor||1
  Cmn2=poll, collect the answers\\into a local database, or both.\\\\Drop||1
  Cmn3=it on every processor. Leave Respond_Mode on and Discover_Mode off||1
  Cmn4=for\\a processor that only answers. Turn Discover_Mode on for the||1
  Cmn5=processor that\\keeps the list. Turn both on when that collector||1
  Cmn6=should also answer polls\\from someone else.\\\\The collector broadcasts||1
  Cmn7=?POLL to 255.255.255.255. Each responder unicasts\\!HERE,MAC,UID,Data||1
  Cmn8=back to the collector. The collector keeps one row per\\UID (or||1
  Cmn9=per MAC, or per IP when those are empty), including itself. Rows\\
  Cmn10=that do not answer the next poll are removed when the window closes.
  Cmn11=\\\\Browse the database with Index. 1 is the first row. Count is||1
  Cmn12=the number of\\rows. Answered_FB is high when the row shown in Processor_*||1
  Cmn13=replied to the\\poll now in progress, or is still in the list after||1
  Cmn14=the window closes.\\\\Leave Respond and Discover unwired to use||1
  Cmn15=Respond_Mode and Discover_Mode.\\After a change on either digital,||1
  Cmn16=that digital takes over and does not fall\\back to the parameter.
  Cmn17=\\\\Poll_Interval 0s polls only when Poll is pulsed. Any other period||1
  Cmn18=also polls\\while Discover is active. A Poll pulse runs one census||1
  Cmn19=even when Discover\\is off. Poll_Window is how long answers are||1
  Cmn20=accepted. Use 3s or more when\\hundreds of processors can reply.
  Cmn21=||1Maximum 512 rows.\\\\Wire format:\\  ?POLL\\  !HERE,00:00:00:00:
  Cmn22=00:00,uid,data\\\\The listen socket stays open on the LAN adapter.
  Cmn23=||1Replies do not retarget it.\\\\-- VERSION HISTORY --\\v1.0  2026-
  Cmn24=10-20\\- Poll, answer, or both, in one symbol\\- Indexed database||1
  Cmn25=of the processors that answered\\
[END]
